Hay que coger avc1 codec compatible con quicktime

./yt-dlp -f 312+234-1 --merge-output-format mp4 "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2nZg4F1pPcc"


Modo auto compatible
./yt-dlp -S "vcodec:h264,res,acodec:m4a" --merge-output-format mp4 "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2nZg4F1pPcc"

Inglés con subtitulos --> 
./yt-dlp -S "lang:en,vcodec:h264,res:1080,acodec:m4a" --write-subs --write-auto-subs --sub-langs "es.*" --embed-subs --merge-output-format mp4 "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2nZg4F1pPcc"
--> si falla hacerlo por pasos:
# Paso 1: vídeo
./yt-dlp -f "bv*[vcodec^=avc1][height<=1080]+ba[ext=m4a][language^=en]/bv*[vcodec^=avc1][height<=1080]+ba[ext=m4a]" \
  --merge-output-format mp4 -o "video.%(ext)s" "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2nZg4F1pPcc"

# Paso 2: solo subtítulos (cuando se pase el límite)
./yt-dlp --skip-download --write-subs --write-auto-subs --sub-langs "es-US-orig" \
  --convert-subs srt --sleep-subtitles 5 -o "video" "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2nZg4F1pPcc"

# Paso 3: incrustarlos para QuickTime
ffmpeg -i video.mp4 -i video.es-US-orig.srt -map 0 -map 1 -c copy -c:s mov_text \
  -metadata:s:s:0 language=spa salida.mp4

